From: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: ipq5332: align NSSCC UNIPHY input order with DT

The IPQ5332 NSSCC clock binding and ipq5332.dtsi both provide each
UNIPHY RX clock before its TX clock. The driver's input-clock enum
reverses those positions, causing the NSS RX clock to select the
UNIPHY TX clock and vice versa. The related IPQ9574 NSSCC driver
already follows the binding order.

Correct only the DT input indices, not the internal hardware parent
mux selectors. On Acer Wave7 the mismatch is visible in debugfs as
port2 RX sourced by PCS::tx_clk and TX by PCS::rx_clk.

This is an isolated A/B test for an intermittent SGMII zero-RX fault,
not proof that the mismatch caused that specific failure.

Signed-off-by: Code and Solder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-ipq5332.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-ipq5332.c
@@ -30,10 +30,10 @@
 	DT_CMN_PLL_NSS_CLK_200M,
 	DT_CMN_PLL_NSS_CLK_300M,
 	DT_GCC_GPLL0_OUT_AUX,
+	DT_UNIPHY0_NSS_RX_CLK,
 	DT_UNIPHY0_NSS_TX_CLK,
-	DT_UNIPHY0_NSS_RX_CLK,
+	DT_UNIPHY1_NSS_RX_CLK,
 	DT_UNIPHY1_NSS_TX_CLK,
-	DT_UNIPHY1_NSS_RX_CLK,
 	DT_XO,
 };
 
